<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battles of Jena and Auerstedt · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-fourth-coalition">War of the Fourth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The twin battles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a> and Auerstedt were fought on 14 October 1806 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> defeated part of the Prussian army at Jena, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-nicolas-davout">Marshal Davout</a> routed the main Prussian force at Auerstedt. The collapse of the Prussian army that followed let French troops enter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> within two weeks, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> lost about half its territory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-tilsit">Peace of Tilsit</a> in 1807.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-jena-auerstedt.jpg" alt="Battle of Jena–Auerstedt" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horace Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iena.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
